# speedandform — Agent context

**Mandatory on every public-facing edit:** [FORM Publication Contract](../../docs/editorial/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md) — **Present the evidence. Don't narrate the presentation.** This includes studies, docs intended for publication, metadata, captions, athlete-facing plans and generated content. No explanatory interface copy, faux-documentary slogans or internal status text. Preserve real source caveats, instructions and cinematic visual identity. Run `node tests/editorial-contract.cjs` and `node scripts/check-editorial-contract.cjs`.

**Standing athlete-first rule (October 19):** **People are the subject. FORM is the platform. The founder is not the narrator.** Remove gratuitous photo credits, repeated coach signatures, `Sent to Brice`, `Brice confirms` and founder-led app marketing. Keep real athlete identities, privacy/tag-review logic, necessary accountability and contractually required credits. Read the [canonical attribution rule](../../docs/editorial/PUBLICATION_CONTRACT.md#athlete-first-attribution--october-19-2026) before app/Network/media/athlete copy. Do not paste the rule itself into public pages.

**Permanent product rule (October 19):** **FORM is an athletic world, not only a schedule. No dead sections.** Before editing homepage/Group/Network/media/athlete cards/notes, read `docs/design/FORM_ATHLETIC_WORLD_STANDARD_2026-10.md` and `docs/product/FORM_ATHLETIC_WORLD_CONTENT_MODEL_2026-10.md`. Do not treat no upcoming run as no content: showcase only eligible real FORM albums, films, consented library photos or approved small notes. Preserve dates, privacy, withdrawn media, truthful RSVP status and the original cinematic entrance. No feed, new UGC system, fabricated event/photo, or duplicate homepage content.

**Approved dramatic bend treatment (October 19):** Read `docs/design/FORM_BEND_PHOTOGRAPHIC_APERTURE_2026-10.md`. Measured nine-lane bend may become a grand photographic aperture around consented real FORM athletes; the actual SF emblem can be composed into the scene; asymmetrical typography and negative space provide atmosphere. The same pattern must not be cloned across every room. Preserve owner-approved visual theater and responsive mobile legibility, avoid generic slogans and stock humans, and do not alter the native launch or deploy by implication.

**Human tone (workspace default):** Site = understanding (philosophical, timeless); still human, not deck-speak. `FORM-iOS/docs/BRICE_OS/HUMAN_TONE_DEFAULT.md`. FORM web spec governs tone split with app.

## Owner-approved visual north star (October 14)

**Always applies to the website, FORM Network and branded media.** This project is **not anti-decoration**. Aim for emotionally resonant athletic editorial cinema: photography, theatre, elegant drama, delight, immersive strips, deep blacks, luminous detail, generous layering, artful gradients, composition and considered motion. Avoid the agent tendency to flatten experiences into text-first cards, stripped-down menus, generic app panels or plain lists. A decorative photograph may remain purely atmospheric; it does not need to be linked.

**Mandatory sources:** `docs/BRAND.md` top active section, `docs/design/FORM_VISUAL_EXECUTION_STANDARD_2026-10.md`, `brand/index.html`, and `AGENTS.md`. Newer owner approval outranks broad historic "no decoration" interpretations. Preserve consent, no fabricated athletes, readability, focus, responsive/Reduce Motion, page weight and no invented data.

For image grading, inspect multiple real frames; tune contrast/brightness/vignette per photo. Keep dramatic rich blacks and living highlights without losing facial detail. Protect copy on phones with layered background shadows instead of deleting hero visual effects. Check actual before/after renders before calling it complete. Do not delete photo strips or motion on aesthetic autopilot.

